invariant: INV-22
file: tcp_nonblocking_frame.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: tcp_nonblocking_fail writes an alert record after the peer's fatal
  alert, so a client stages one for ch_record_out and a server pushes one, and
  each answers an alert that closed the connection, which RFC 9846 section 6.2
  forbids. bin/tcp_nonblocking_loop_test requires both ends to stage and push
  nothing after it.

--- old
    uint8_t alert = r->t.alert_received == 0 ? r->hs.alert : 0;
--- new
    uint8_t alert = r->hs.alert;
